  "result": "I re-planned `NRS-484B-413-2` and wrote the three files. The validator now accepts both the node `NRS_484B_413_2` and the concept record `drv.lane.heading_left_of_carrier`.\n\n- **Why it came back:** the plan used `drv.lane.heading_left_of_carrier` for span s6 (\"prior to changing the course\") but did not include its concept record. The validator had rejected that concept because its argument sorts and atoms match the accepted `drv.lane.heading_right_of_carrier`.\n- **The fix:** I proposed the left concept again as the mirror of the right one, with a `differs_from` entry. The right concept's contract explicitly excludes a heading turned to the left. Its arguments are a road user and a region, so neither swapping nor negating them gives the left side. A left/right argument wouldn't help either, because the formula language can't compare such an argument with a spelling. So the two sides have to be separate concepts, and the law needs both because the signal must show the side the vehicle turns to.\n- **One wording change in the obligation:** the previous record picked the 100 ft or 300 ft distance window with a conditional inside the window length. A window length must be a constant term, so I split it into two branches: business or residential district with the 100 ft window, otherwise the 300 ft window.\n- **Everything else is unchanged** from the iteration-1 record: the text cuts, atom mappings, district assumption, the weather sentence treated as adding no restriction, the scenarios and the two stated distances.\n\n**Remaining risk:** the trigger only applies when the vehicle occupies some lane; everywhere else it reads as unknown. If the gate finds this makes ordinary trips through intersections unknown, the trigger would need to be re-read over any occupied road region that has a designated direction.\n\n`PLAN.md` also has a note for the operator: mirror-image concepts like these two will always trip the duplicate-concept check. Each such law will need a `differs_from` entry until the language has a way to pass a side the concept can read.\n\nFiles are in the plan directory:\n- `blueprint.jsonl`\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `aggregates.jsonl` (empty; this law defines no aggregate of its own)",
